Created by openclaw -> lm studio -> qwen3.8-27b

Might work for any jvc projector that listens on tcp port 20554.
Let me know if it does.

python .\jvcpjctl.py -h
usage: jvcpjctl [-h] [--ip IP] [{on,off}]

Control a JVC DLT-20 (DLA) projector over LAN.

positional arguments:
  {on,off}    power on / off (default: query status)

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --ip IP     projector IP address (default: 192.168.1.200)

Example usage:

python .\jvcpjctl.py --ip 192.168.1.200
Projector at 192.168.1.200: Standby (off)

python .\jvcpjctl.py --ip 192.168.1.200 on
Projector at 192.168.1.200: power on command accepted

python .\jvcpjctl.py --ip 192.168.1.200 off
Projector at 192.168.1.200: power off command accepted
